@startuml
participant "Alice main\nthread" as AM
participant "Alice\nlanlink-\nclient-reader" as AR
participant "Alice\nlanlink-\nfile-sender" as AS
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id›\n(Alice)" as SA
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id›\n(Bob)" as SB
participant "Bob\nlanlink-\nclient-reader" as BR
participant "Bob main\nthread" as BM

note over AM, AR
∕offer bob a.pdf → inspect_file:
size + SHA-256 of the whole file
end note
AM ->> SA : FILE_OFFER (transfer_id, recipient,\nfilename, size, sha256, chunk_size)
note over SA, SB
TransferSession
OFFERED
end note
SA ->> BR : FILE_OFFER (+ sender)
BR ->> BM : event
note over BM
∕accept ‹id›
accept_file:
Receiver.start
opens .part file
end note
BM ->> SB : FILE_ACCEPT (transfer_id)
note over SA, SB : ACCEPTED
SB ->> AR : FILE_ACCEPT
SB ->> BR : FILE_ACCEPT echo
note over AR
SendSession
ACCEPTED
end note
AR ->> AS : start thread
AR ->> AM : event
BR ->> BM : event

loop seq = 0 … n−1, SendSession.outgoing()
  AS ->> SA : FILE_CHUNK\n(seq, data)
  note over SA, SB
  _relay_file_content
  TRANSFERRING
  end note
  SA ->> BR : FILE_CHUNK (seq, data)
  note over BR
  Receiver.write:
  seq == expected,
  size check,
  append, hash,
  progress bar
  end note
end
AS ->> SA : FILE_END
note over SA, SB : VERIFYING
SA ->> BR : FILE_END (total_chunks,\ntotal_bytes)
note over BR
Receiver.finish:
counts, SHA-256
== offer.sha256,
fsync, rename
.part → final
end note
BR ->> BM : final snapshot
BR ->> SB : FILE_RESULT\n(ok = true,\nreceived_bytes,\nsha256)
note over SA, SB
COMPLETED,
session removed
end note
SB ->> AR : FILE_RESULT
note over AR
SendSession
checks size
and sha256:
COMPLETED
end note
AR ->> AM : final snapshot
note over AM, BM
No per-chunk ACK: TCP flow control paces the sender thread.
The server relays chunks without reading the file content.
"event" and "final snapshot" are items put on that client's
commands queue and printed by its main thread.
end note
@enduml
